remarks.para:
Where the glass copied the frame's picture this frame (), the pass reads that copy too,
sharp and blurred, so a hit can tear the picture on the side it came from. Only the pixels a hit touches are laid back;
everywhere else the picture under the display is left as it was drawn.

member.remarks:
The interface's shaders, which composite as the original did: their colours are authored at the
display encoding and blended there. Every RHI texture's sampler decodes, so a texel is put back;
and a target that encodes as it stores is handed its colour decoded, so it is encoded once.
